repository-code: https://github.com/rgrimson/cubetas-morphometry
abstract: >-
  Code and derived data supporting a census-scale analysis of 3210 cubetas
  (shallow closed depressions) in the upper Matanza-Riachuelo and Reconquista
  basins, on the loessic plain of northeastern Buenos Aires Province, Argentina.
  The pipeline covers planimetric morphometry, axial circular statistics and
  von Mises mixture model selection, Ripley point-pattern analysis, effect-size
  comparisons of slope and drainage position, and the coupling between cubeta
  orientation and the orientation of the surrounding valley field. The LiDAR
  digital elevation models the analysis derives from are not distributed; only
  the point-wise quantities extracted from them are.
keywords:
  - cubetas
  - closed depressions
  - Pampa plain
  - morphometry
  - circular statistics
  - spatial point-pattern analysis
  - landscape hydrology
  - wetlands
